# Intent: Swipe pages, part 2: the pure data and layout. hal/maipai_pages_core.h holds the six page types (clock, timers, games, actions, frame, tiles; each at most once, three on each side of the face, the clock on the left and the games on the right until the owner chooses), the quick actions (find, beep, dance, game, hello; four to six), the control sheet items (two sliders, up to seven buttons and four status lines out of volume, brightness, mute, quiet, light, find, timers, games, wifi, battery, tailnet, address), the closing times, the saved text line under the one flash key pages_cfg (9 characters; a damaged value reads as the defaults), every setter all or nothing with a plain sentence, the host fed tiles (up to six: icon, label up to 12 and value up to 10 plain characters; the flash write is rate limited to once in ten minutes), ten drawn icons as shapes in a 24 by 24 box (no icon font), and the layout of the sheet (it covers about the lower 60 percent of the screen, never the banner row; tiles 72 by 38, sliders two to a row) and of the page contents inside the face zone (y 28 to 184). Plain C99, no heap, no clock. Nothing is wired yet.
# Placement: unit (pure data; the settings page preview and the host table are checked equal to it)
